# 1. Scope, objective, invariants

## 1.1 Actuator classes, ordered by reversibility

The plan phases by reversibility class, not by glamour:

```
R0 — reversible, cheap:      node sleep/wake; antenna pointing; RIS state
R1 — reversible, costly:     mobile relay repositioning (energy to return)
R2 — committed:              deploying a physical charger/beacon/relay;
                             battery-irreversible expenditures; abandonment
```

## 1.2 Objective

Let `g` denote the geometry state (positions, deployed assets, RIS/antenna
states, sleep set). Tier 11 maximizes

```
V(g) − price-weighted actuation cost(g_old → g)                        (T11.1)
```

where `V(g)` is the certified Tier ≤10 mission objective at geometry `g`
(the existing stack evaluated as an oracle), and the actuation cost is priced
through the Tier 10 ledger (joules × energy price; R2 commitments × their
shadow value). Decomposable, cheaply-computable components of `V` used for
search guidance (not for certification): Γ(g) — one Dijkstra; the
harvest-desert map — thresholds against the incident field; the ν_w field —
closed form at the converged solution; per-node attrition margins
`(d_{b,w}/d_{i,w})^α` in contested cells.

## 1.3 Invariants (MUST)

- **I11.1 — No actuation outside a certified MotionEnvelope.** The Tier 6
  authority pattern lifted to actuators: pre-certified zones, speed/energy
  caps, machine-checkable safety predicates, expiry.
- **I11.2 — R2 actions require external authority, always.** Committed
  (irreversible) acts never auto-execute under any envelope; human or
  Tier 10-style signed policy with the R2 flag, and a ReversibilityLedger
  entry before execution.
- **I11.3 — Actuation energy is charged against StabilityCertificate
  margins.** A move that would violate any node's certified energy margin
  (D9) is infeasible by construction, not by hope.
- **I11.4 — Every move invalidates the gain calibration it touches.**
  Post-move, all gain-operator entries involving moved/deployed assets revert
  to widened (free-space + inflation) bounds until re-calibrated (§4.5).
  Planning that ignores this books value it has not yet earned.
- **I11.5 — Proposals carry trust regions.** The geometry gradient is local;
  route-switch boundaries break it; every quoted ΔV carries the re-solve-
  verified region, exactly the Tier 10 U1 pattern with geometry as the
  perturbed quantity.
- **I11.6 — Hysteresis.** Dwell times per asset; no asset moves twice within
  its dwell; oscillating proposal pairs are suppressed.

