```

The gradient row deserves emphasis: moving node `w` changes *both* its link
distances `d_{u,w}, d_{w,v}` *and* its harvest/interference position
`d_{i,w}` — all entering the closed-form cost as powers of distances, so
∂T/∂x_w is exact within a fixed route. The discrete hazard is the route
switching under the move; hence I11.5's trust regions, computed by re-solve
at perturbed positions (warm-started, Ring-0 cheap).

