# 6. Staging and milestones

```
M0  GeometryValueService (2 wks) — observability only.
    Desert maps, Γ, ν_w fields, attrition margins as dashboards/ledger rows.
    Standalone value: operators see where the network is starving and exposed.
M1  Deploy-time PlacementTool (3 wks) — offline recommendations.
    U1 with the robust (jammer-scenario) variant; greedy-vs-MILP gap report.
    Zero runtime risk; immediately useful for the next physical deployment.
M2  R0 actuation (2–3 wks) — sleep/wake (+ antenna/RIS where present) under
    envelopes; SHADOW first (proposals ledgered, not executed), then
    LIMITED-ACTIVE. The cheapest live test of the whole gate/ledger chain.
M3  R1 mobile moves (3–4 wks) — gradient generator, trust regions,
    calibration debt accounting (§4.5) live; human-gated first, envelope-
    bound after the T11 audit deck passes.
M4  R2 deployment proposals (2 wks) — U1-on-live-field proposals through the
    external-authority path; ReversibilityLedger drills.
M5  Robust placement ↔ Tier 9 integration — jammer-position scenarios from
    the equilibrium layer's q*; Γ-mixture evaluation. (Integration milestone.)
```

Critical path M0→M2 ≈ 6–7 weeks to first live (reversible) actuation. M1 is
the highest value-to-risk item in the entire tier and should ship even if
runtime actuation never does.

